---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
List boards and folders as a tree, or as another view.
It prints one line per node with its link.
--view recent is per account across workspaces; -w does not filter it.

USAGE
  holst board ls [flags]

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws    Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --folder folder   List only this folder: a folder id, link or part of its name; / is the root; the whole workspace by default
      --view view       Which boards: tree, trash, both, favorites, recent or sidebar; tree by default
  -l, --limit n         At most this many nodes; 0 shows all; all by default
      --cursor cursor   Continue after this cursor, as the end of the previous page printed it; the first page by default

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b ls -w easy
  $ holst b ls -w easy --folder "Plans" -l 20
  $ holst b ls --view recent

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
